tle ? '' : 'esh-pan esh-mod' + (name === 'map' ? ' esh-wide' : ''));\n    sh.appendChild(box); sh.setAttribute('role', 'dialog'); sh.setAttribute('aria-label', v(s.title || s.name) || name);\n    const add = (...c) => box.append(...c.filter(Boolean));\n    add(s.emblem && this._el('div', 'esh-emb', s.emblem), s.kicker && this._el('div', 'esh-k', v(s.kicker)));\n    if (title) add(this._el('h1', '', v(s.name || s.title)), s.subtitle && this._el('div', 'esh-sub', v(s.subtitle)));\n    else add(this._el('h2', '', v(s.title) || { pause: this._game._players && this._game._players.length > 1 && this._game.pausedBy ? 'Paused by P' + this._game.pausedBy : 'Paused', settings: 'Settings', controls: 'Controls', help: 'Help', map: 'Map' }[name] || ''));   // (several players: who paused)\n    add(v(s.text) && this._el('p', title ? '' : 'esh-m', v(s.text)));\n    for (const key of v(s.rows) || []) add(key[0] === '#' ? this._el('div', 'esh-k esh-sec', key.slice(1)) : this._row(key));   // (setting rows on a screen of the game's own: '#' a heading)\n    if (name === 'settings') this._settingsRows(add);\n    if (name === 'controls') this._controls(add);\n    if (s.keys) { const g = this._el('div', 'esh-grid'); for (const [k, w] of v(s.keys)) g.append(this._el('kbd', '', k), this._el('span', '', w)); add(g); }\n    for (const [h, t] of v(s.sections) || []) add(this._el('div', 'esh-k esh-sec', h), this._el('p', 'esh-m', t));\n    if (s.stats) { const g = this._el('div', 'esh-stats'); for (const [val, lab] of v(s.stats)) { const c = this._el('div'); c.append(this._el('b', '', val), this._el('small', '', lab)); g.appendChild(c); } add(g); }\n    if (s.medals) { const g = this._el('div'); for (const [lab, got] of v(s.medals)) g.appendChild(this._el('span', 'esh-med' + (got ? '' : ' off'), (got ? '✓ ' : '') + lab)); add(g); }\n129:- `E.V3.rz(v, a)`: v turned by angle a (radians) about the z axis\n243:- `view.yawDeg`: the turn about the up axis, degrees (0: north is up the screen; iso is 45)\n338:- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n503:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n789:- `map.wall(from, dir, o = {})` †: the wall face a body touches or faces: from `from`, in direction dir (an angle or [dx, dy]), the first point within reach whose top rises more than a step above its  [... omitted end of long line]\n1048:- `E.pattern.aim(a, b, speed)`: aim from a to b on the ground plane (x, y); aimSide uses x, z\n1467:- `grid.face(a, b)`: the way from a looks to b, one of four [dx, dy] (the longer axis; x when they tie): a unit turning to its target\nclass Menu {\n  constructor(game, items, o = {}) {\n    /** game: its game; items: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled }); i: the one under the cursor; active:\n     *  false stops it reading input */\n    this.game = game; this.items = items || []; this.i = 0; this.active = true;\n    /** x, y: where it sits, 'center' or pixels; title: a heading, or null; box: draw a window round it; color: the\n     *  entries' color; pick: the color of the one under the cursor; dim: disabled entries' color; bg, border: the\n     *  window's colors; onPick: called (i, item) on confirm; onCancel: called on cancel; onMove: called (i, item)\n     *  when the cursor moves; sound: false silences it; input: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so\n     *  any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's); scale: its text and rows that many times (2, 3:\n     *  across a room on a TV); rows: at most that many entries shown, the list scrolling under its cursor (0: all) */\n    Object.assign(this, { x: 'center', y: 'center', title: null, box: true, color: '#ffffff', pick: '#ffd36a', dim: '#6a6488', bg: '#141a3a', border: '#e8e4ff', onPick: null, onCancel: null, onMove: null, sound: true, input: null, scale: 1, rows: 0 }, o);\n    this._skip(1);\n  }\n  _label(it) { return typeof it === 'stri